# ai.wing — Change Log & Architecture Record

Running record of structural changes, feature additions and architectural
decisions for the Sonic Authorized Retailer landing site. Newest entries at the
bottom. Each entry should be specific enough to reverse.

---

## [0.1.0] — Initial build

### Stack
- Next.js 16.3.5 (App Router) · React 19.2.8 · TypeScript 5 · Tailwind CSS v4
- `lenis` for smooth scrolling. No other runtime dependencies.
- Strict frontend build: no API routes, no database, no server actions.

### Architectural decisions

**1. `lib/content.ts` is the single source of truth.**
Every dollar amount, speed, fee, promotional qualifier, feature bullet, FAQ
answer and legal disclosure lives in this one module. No `.tsx` file contains a
hard-coded price, speed or plan name. Changing a rate there cascades to the hero
price anchor, every plan card, the fine-print comparison table and the footer
disclosures with zero layout edits.

Derived helpers keep layout files data-free:
- `plansFor(line)` — plans on one service line
- `activeServiceLines()` — lines that have plans, in canonical order
- `leadPlan()` — the hero price anchor (flagged popular fiber plan)
- `formatSpeed()` / `speedLabel()` — 10000 → "10 Gig", symmetry-aware
- `hasPrice()` / `ctaLabel()` — drives "Call to order" vs "Call for pricing"
- `finePrintTable()` — builds the comparison grid rows from `PLANS`

**2. Service lines render by data presence, not by hand.**
`SERVICE_LINE_ORDER` fixes the merchandising order as
`fiber → cable → bundle → tv → mobile → phone`. `ServiceSections.tsx` maps over
`activeServiceLines()`, which filters out any line with zero plans. Adding a
cable plan to `PLANS` would make a cable section appear in the correct slot with
no component change; removing the last plan on a line deletes its section.

**3. `<PriceLockup plan={plan} />` is the only price presentation.**
A flex row of raised dollar sign, dominant integer and muted cents, with the
promotional qualifier beneath. Two sizes (`card` = 2.5rem integer, `hero` =
2.75–3.5rem responsive) and two tones (`light`, `dark`). When a plan has no
`price`, it renders "Call for pricing" instead — the same condition that flips
the card's CTA wording. Includes an `sr-only` spoken price so screen readers do
not read the split lockup as three fragments.

**4. `<CallButton />` owns every telephone CTA.**
Centralises the `tel:` href and guarantees the `data-call-cta` tracking
attribute on every call action. The two inline `tel:` links that are not buttons
(hero subline, footer number) and the header/ZIP-result buttons also carry
`data-call-cta`.

### Content audit against sonic.com

Plans, rates and fees were taken from Sonic's own site and availability results:

| Service line | Status | Source finding |
|---|---|---|
| Fiber | **Included** | 10 Gigabit fiber, $49.99/mo intro for 12 mos., $59.99/mo after; free install; symmetrical; unlimited data; no contract. Pre-order tier for neighborhoods under construction (no published rate → "Call for pricing"). |
| Cable | **Omitted** | Sonic sells fiber-to-the-home only; cable appears on its site solely as a competitor technology. |
| Bundle | **Included** | Sonic Fusion Fiber 1 Gig, $49.99/mo intro / $59.99/mo after, 940 Mbps typical each way, ~3 ms latency, includes one home phone line. |
| TV | **Omitted** | Sonic's own TV page states it does not sell streaming devices or services; it recommends third-party Roku + YouTube TV. Not a native service, so the section does not exist. |
| Mobile | **Omitted** | No consumer mobile service. "Sonic Mobile Communicator" is a softphone app for an existing home phone line, not mobile service — it is listed as a Fusion feature instead. |
| Phone | **Included** | Sonic Home Phone / Sonic Voice, $10/mo added to Fusion fiber; unlimited nationwide calling plus 70 countries; Nomorobo spam blocking; number transfer; ATA provided. |

Equipment (optional, never required): Sonic WiFi 7 $5/mo · WiFi Pro 7 $10/mo ·
WiFi Max 7 $20/mo. Universal terms: $0 install, $0 one-time fees, $0 early
termination, $0/GB overage.

### Compliance constraints enforced
- Persistent, non-dismissable disclosure bar: "Independent Authorized Retailer
  of Sonic." Sticky with the header, so it stays on screen for the whole scroll.
- Hero keeps **both** the ZIP availability checker and a call button.
- Body CTAs read "Call to order", or "Call for pricing" when a plan has no
  published rate. Raw phone numbers appear only in the header and footer.
- No carrier support routing — no instruction to contact Sonic for billing,
  outages or support anywhere on the page.
- No empty sections, no "call to ask" placeholder cards for services Sonic does
  not offer.
- No Broadband Facts label links. No "pricing observed" date stamps. No
  "is this the official site?" FAQ. No competitor bashing and no
  self-deprecating copy about being an ordering channel.
- ZIP checker makes no availability claim: a valid ZIP reveals a next step,
  since serviceability is decided at the street address.

### Design notes
- Palette: Sonic Vibrant Blue `#00A4E4` (with `#0092CC` hover and `#007BAD` deep
  for text-on-light contrast), dark slate `#0B131D` surfaces, white, and a
  neutral grey ramp. Defined as Tailwind v4 `@theme` tokens in `app/globals.css`.
  > **Superseded in [0.2.0].** `#00A4E4` came from the brief and is not the blue
  > Sonic actually ships. The palette was re-derived by sampling screenshots of
  > sonic.com — see [0.2.0] for the measured values now in use.
- Typography: Inter via `next/font`, tight tracking on headings.
- Motion: Lenis smooth scroll with anchor interception; one-shot
  `IntersectionObserver` entrance reveals that unobserve after firing; hover
  lifts on cards. No WebGL, no 3D backgrounds, no animated diagrams. Everything
  is disabled under `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- FAQ uses native `<details>`/`<summary>` so it works without JavaScript.
- `overflow-x: clip` on `html`/`body` plus `min-width: 0` on all elements; the
  fine-print table is swapped for stacked cards below `lg` rather than being put
  in a horizontal scroller, which keeps 320px free of horizontal overflow.

### Known placeholder
`SITE.phoneDisplay` / `SITE.phoneHref` in `lib/content.ts` hold
`(888) 555-0123`. The 555-01xx range is reserved and never connects. **Replace
with the retailer's own tracked sales number before launch** — it must not be a
carrier support line.

