## [0.3.1] — Hero availability control slimmed, duplicate call CTA removed

**Requested:** drop the "Prefer to speak with someone / Call to order" block from
the hero, and shrink the oversized availability bar.

**Compliance check first.** The standing rule is that the hero must carry BOTH a
ZIP checker and a call button. Removing the bar's CTA is safe because the hero
still contains the "Call to order" button inside `<HeroPlanPlate>` — the rule is
about the section, not that specific control. Verified in the DOM: the `#hero`
subtree contains exactly one `tel:` link ("CALL TO ORDER — SONIC FIBER 10 GIG")
and one `input[autocomplete="postal-code"]`. `Hero.tsx`'s docblock now states
this explicitly so the call action is not removed by accident later.

**Changes**
- `ZipChecker.tsx` rebuilt as a compact control: the label sits on the dark hero
  stage and only the field itself is a white pill (`p-2`, `py-2.5` input and
  button). It no longer renders a persistent call button.
- Moved out of the full-width docked bar and into the copy column, between the
  subline and the trust chips, capped at `max-w-xl`.
- Desktop footprint went from a full-container card (~1088px wide, tall enough
  to hold a label, an input row and a second CTA column) to **576 × 59px**.
  At 320px it stacks to 280 × 105px.
- The post-check result panel is retained — it appears only after a valid ZIP is
  entered, and restyled to sit on the dark hero rather than as a white card. Its
  phone link keeps `data-call-cta`.

**QA:** `tsc`, `eslint`, `next build` clean and still fully static. No horizontal
overflow at 320px. Site-wide `tel:` links now 9, all 9 carrying `data-call-cta`
(down from 10 — the removed control).

