## [0.7.2] — Fusion card banner matched to the supplied reference

A screenshot of the target pattern was supplied. Two differences from [0.7.1]:

- **Banner proportion.** The reference banner measures roughly 2.3:1; ours was
  `aspect-[16/9]` (1.78). Changed to `aspect-[21/9]` (2.33) — 672×288 at desktop
  instead of 672×378. Keeps 79% of the 1.83:1 source height.
- **Bottom edge.** The reference dissolves the photograph into the card surface;
  ours ended on a hairline `border-b`. Replaced with an 80px white gradient
  (transparent → 0.72 → solid) pinned to the bottom of the banner, and the
  border removed, so the image reads as part of the card rather than a plate
  stuck on top of it.

Rounded top corners come from the card's existing `overflow: hidden` +
`rounded-[18px]`, so the banner inherits them without extra rules.

Verified in the rendered DOM: banner 672×288 (2.33), flush with the card top,
80px fade anchored to the banner's bottom edge, `border-bottom-width: 0px`,
card radius 18px with `overflow: hidden`.

**Still not visually confirmed** — the Browser pane returned blank captures
throughout.

