## [1.2.0] — Footer rebuilt to the bestfiberinternet.us layout

Their footer was measured from its rendered DOM rather than eyeballed, because
the earlier text-only description of it had the column order wrong.

**What they actually do** (footer 1425×1168):

| Element | Position | Type |
|---|---|---|
| Brand + blurb | column 1, x=144 | lead block, not a trailing column |
| SHOP | x=493 | 12.8px / weight 800 / uppercase / 1.536px tracking |
| LEARN | x=753 | same |
| TALK TO A HUMAN | x=1012 | heading + large phone + hours + mailing address |
| OFFER DETAILS & REQUIRED DISCLOSURES | x=144, y=327, full width | labelled heading above the fine print |
| Policy links | y=1015 | single horizontal row |

**What changed here**
- The brand lockup moved from column 4 to column 1; grid is now
  `[1.5fr_1fr_1fr_1.25fr]`.
- "Order by phone" became **Talk to a human**, with the number at 22px and the
  mailing address added beneath the hours.
- The fine print gained the **"Offer details & required disclosures"** heading —
  previously it was an unlabelled block of grey text.
- The separate "Policies" grid became a single horizontal row in the bottom bar,
  matching theirs. All eight fit on one row at desktop.
- Column headings adopted their weight and tracking: `font-extrabold`,
  `uppercase`, `tracking-[0.12em]`.
- Contact email added opposite the copyright.

**Kept deliberately:** the Sonic navy (`#10132B`) rather than their `#001226`.
The request was for their layout; the palette was sampled from sonic.com and
stays.

Verified against the reference — headings land at x=514/758/1002 versus their
493/753/1012, at 13px/800/1.56px versus 12.8px/800/1.536px.

### QA
- `tsc`, `eslint`, `next build` clean; 12 routes, all static.
- Desktop 1440: no overflow, 8 policy links on one row, copyright still
  year-less.
- Mobile 375: no page or footer overflow, every footer link ≥31px tall, the
  `tel:` link still carries `data-call-cta`.
